WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.310
Insurance.

2
00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:05.899
Day 39 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:07.649 --> 00:00:08.673
The key idea.

4
00:00:08.953 --> 00:00:19.300
Today's goal: ask the right questions before buying health, life, motor or travel insurance, make a claim clearly, and follow up when a claim is delayed or rejected.

5
00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:21.418
Info:

6
00:00:21.698 --> 00:00:23.127
Read the policy wording.

7
00:00:23.407 --> 00:00:27.802
Cover, exclusions and claim rules depend on the insurer and the plan.

8
00:00:28.082 --> 00:00:35.207
Before buying, ask for the policy wording and exclusions in writing, and check claims with the insurer's official helpline.

9
00:00:36.557 --> 00:00:37.411
Part 1.

10
00:00:37.691 --> 00:00:38.651
Key words.

11
00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:41.245
Here is a quick table:

12
00:00:41.525 --> 00:01:02.282
Word or phrase, and Meaning. premium: what you pay (monthly or yearly). sum insured or cover: the maximum the insurer pays. policyholder or insured or nominee: who owns it or who's covered or who receives money. term plan or health or motor or travel insurance: policy types. waiting period: time

13
00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:14.167
before some illnesses are covered. pre-existing disease (PED): illness you had before buying. exclusions: what is NOT covered. co-pay or deductible: your share of the bill.

14
00:01:15.517 --> 00:01:37.085
cashless or reimbursement: insurer pays the hospital or you pay and claim later. network hospital or garage: partner hospital or garage for cashless claims. no-claim bonus (NCB): discount or extra cover for years without claims. claim settlement or rejection or grievance: outcome of a claim or complaint.

15
00:01:38.435 --> 00:01:39.310
Part 2.

16
00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:41.361
Questions to ask before buying.

17
00:01:42.611 --> 00:01:43.315
Health.

18
00:01:43.595 --> 00:01:46.560
What is the waiting period for pre-existing diseases?

19
00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.165
Is there a room-rent limit or co-payment?

20
00:01:49.445 --> 00:01:52.389
Which hospitals near me are in the cashless network?

21
00:01:52.669 --> 00:01:56.019
Are maternity or OPD or day-care treatments covered?

22
00:01:56.299 --> 00:01:57.835
What are the main exclusions?

23
00:01:58.115 --> 00:02:00.419
Is the premium likely to increase with age?

24
00:02:01.769 --> 00:02:02.750
Life (term).

25
00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:05.910
How much cover do you recommend for my income and loans?

26
00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:08.195
Until what age does the cover last?

27
00:02:08.475 --> 00:02:10.651
What happens if I miss a premium payment?

28
00:02:10.931 --> 00:02:13.641
What is the claim settlement ratio of the insurer?

29
00:02:14.991 --> 00:02:16.164
Motor and travel.

30
00:02:16.444 --> 00:02:18.471
Is zero depreciation included?

31
00:02:18.751 --> 00:02:20.692
Is roadside assistance included?

32
00:02:20.972 --> 00:02:24.172
How does the no-claim bonus work if I make a small claim?

33
00:02:24.452 --> 00:02:29.039
(Travel) Does it cover medical emergencies, flight delays and lost baggage?

34
00:02:29.319 --> 00:02:32.284
(Travel) Is it accepted for my visa application?

35
00:02:33.634 --> 00:02:34.530
Part 3.

36
00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:37.370
Conversation 1: buying health insurance.

37
00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:40.647
Here is how the conversation goes.

38
00:02:40.927 --> 00:02:43.785
Hello, this is Rohan from SafeLife Insurance.

39
00:02:44.065 --> 00:02:46.625
You requested a callback about health insurance.

40
00:02:46.905 --> 00:02:47.951
Yes, thanks.

41
00:02:48.231 --> 00:02:52.092
I'm looking for a family floater for me, my wife and my son.

42
00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:53.076
Sure.

43
00:02:53.356 --> 00:02:55.020
What cover are you looking for?

44
00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.028
About 10 lakh rupees.

45
00:02:57.308 --> 00:03:02.855
Before we talk about the price, could you tell me the waiting period for pre-existing diseases?

46
00:03:04.205 --> 00:03:05.805
The conversation continues.

47
00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:11.290
Three years for pre-existing diseases, and 30 days for new illnesses, except accidents.

48
00:03:11.570 --> 00:03:13.234
My wife has thyroid.

49
00:03:13.514 --> 00:03:15.711
Will that be covered after three years?

50
00:03:15.991 --> 00:03:17.591
Yes, if you declare it now.

51
00:03:17.871 --> 00:03:20.538
Is there a room-rent limit or a co-payment?

52
00:03:20.818 --> 00:03:24.167
No room-rent limit, and no co-payment below age 60.

53
00:03:25.517 --> 00:03:27.117
The conversation continues.

54
00:03:27.397 --> 00:03:30.064
Which hospitals near Whitefield are cashless?

55
00:03:30.344 --> 00:03:31.859
I'll email you the list.

56
00:03:32.139 --> 00:03:35.083
The premium is about 21,000 rupeesa year.

57
00:03:35.363 --> 00:03:39.544
Could you also email the policy wording and the list of exclusions?

58
00:03:39.824 --> 00:03:42.085
I'd like to read them before deciding.

59
00:03:42.365 --> 00:03:44.328
Sure, I'll send everything today.

60
00:03:45.678 --> 00:03:46.595
Part 4.

61
00:03:46.875 --> 00:03:49.926
Conversation 2: following up on a delayed claim.

62
00:03:51.176 --> 00:03:53.203
Here is how the conversation goes.

63
00:03:53.483 --> 00:03:54.848
Thank you for calling.

64
00:03:55.128 --> 00:03:56.387
How can I help you?

65
00:03:56.667 --> 00:03:57.392
Hi.

66
00:03:57.672 --> 00:04:02.152
I submitted a reimbursement claim three weeks ago, and there's no update.

67
00:04:02.432 --> 00:04:07.403
The claim number is CLM-448190.

68
00:04:07.683 --> 00:04:08.792
Let me check...

69
00:04:09.072 --> 00:04:11.888
It's pending because the discharge summary is missing.

70
00:04:12.168 --> 00:04:13.981
I uploaded it on the 5th.

71
00:04:14.261 --> 00:04:15.840
Could you check again, please?

72
00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.790
The conversation continues.

73
00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.777
You're right, I can see it now.

74
00:04:21.057 --> 00:04:22.635
It wasn't linked to the claim.

75
00:04:22.915 --> 00:04:24.003
I'll link it.

76
00:04:24.283 --> 00:04:25.222
Thank you.

77
00:04:25.502 --> 00:04:27.657
How long will the settlement take now?

78
00:04:27.937 --> 00:04:29.622
Within seven working days.

79
00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:34.105
Could you send me an email confirming that the documents are complete?

80
00:04:34.385 --> 00:04:35.835
Yes, I'll send it now.

81
00:04:37.185 --> 00:04:38.785
The conversation continues.

82
00:04:39.065 --> 00:04:42.159
And if it's rejected, what's the grievance process?

83
00:04:42.439 --> 00:04:44.316
You can write to our grievance team.

84
00:04:44.596 --> 00:04:46.324
The details are in the email.

85
00:04:46.604 --> 00:04:47.884
Thank you, Priya.

86
00:04:48.164 --> 00:04:49.593
That's very helpful.

87
00:04:50.943 --> 00:04:51.903
Part 5.

88
00:04:52.183 --> 00:04:53.357
When things go wrong.

89
00:04:54.607 --> 00:05:00.025
My claim was rejected as a pre-existing disease, but I declared it when I bought the policy.

90
00:05:00.305 --> 00:05:01.564
I'd like it reviewed.

91
00:05:01.844 --> 00:05:04.831
The hospital says the cashless approval hasn't come yet.

92
00:05:05.111 --> 00:05:06.028
Could you check?

93
00:05:06.308 --> 00:05:08.655
My premium has gone up by 40%.

94
00:05:08.935 --> 00:05:10.215
Could you explain why?

95
00:05:10.495 --> 00:05:13.332
I'd like to port my policy to another insurer.

96
00:05:13.612 --> 00:05:14.807
What's the process?

97
00:05:16.157 --> 00:05:17.095
Part 6.

98
00:05:17.375 --> 00:05:18.293
Practice.

99
00:05:19.543 --> 00:05:24.471
Write 5 questions you'd ask before buying a health insurance policy for your parents.

100
00:05:25.821 --> 00:05:26.738
Success:

101
00:05:27.018 --> 00:05:28.170
Sample answers.

102
00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:31.223
What's the waiting period for pre-existing diseases?

103
00:05:31.503 --> 00:05:33.701
Is there a co-payment for senior citizens?

104
00:05:33.981 --> 00:05:35.495
Is there a room-rent limit?

105
00:05:35.775 --> 00:05:38.101
Which hospitals near their home are cashless?

106
00:05:38.381 --> 00:05:40.706
How much will the premium increase each year?

107
00:05:42.056 --> 00:05:42.995
Part 7.

108
00:05:43.275 --> 00:05:44.320
Speak today.

109
00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:49.666
Find your own policy number and claim helpline, and save them in your phone.

110
00:05:49.946 --> 00:05:54.383
Explain in 2 sentences what your health insurance covers and doesn't cover.

111
00:05:55.733 --> 00:05:57.269
That's the end of this lesson.

112
00:05:57.549 --> 00:06:02.200
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

113
00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:08.603
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

